## Error Handling

### HTTP Errors
- **catchError** in services, not components
  ```typescript
  createOrder(order: CreateOrderRequest): Observable<OrderResponse> {
    return this.http.post<OrderResponse>('/orders', order).pipe(
      catchError((error: HttpErrorResponse) => {
        console.error('Order creation failed:', error);
        this.toastService.error('Failed to create order');
        return throwError(() => new Error('Order creation failed'));
      })
    );
  }
  ```

### User-Friendly Messages
- Display errors in UI (toasts, inline messages, error pages)
- Don't leak internal details to users

